# Gebeta Full-Stack Rules

- Read the root AGENTS.md before implementation.
- Inspect existing code before modifying it.
- Build a real integrated application, not a frontend-only prototype.
- Use React, TypeScript, and Vite for the frontend.
- Use Node.js and Express for the backend.
- Use Supabase Auth for authentication.
- Use Supabase PostgreSQL for persistent data.
- Use Supabase Storage for images.
- Use real Express API endpoints for business operations.
- Verify Supabase-issued access tokens in the backend.
- Enforce backend authorization and database RLS.
- Keep service-role and AI credentials on the backend.
- Do not use hardcoded arrays as substitutes for core database functionality.
- Do not invent endpoints, database fields, or integrations.
- Do not introduce fake authentication or fake database services.
- Keep demo workflows simple, but fully functional.
- Use realistic database seed data for demonstration.
- Clearly label AI fallbacks and nutritional estimates.
- Update documentation when implementation changes.
- Test actual frontend/backend integration.
- Do not claim untested functionality works.
